WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
BUILD 068. FROM KNOWING YOU TO ACTING FOR YOU. A passive fixed synthetic model can suggest context and prepare a bounded proposal. Knowledge alone never supplies authority.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
ADD THE RUNTIME. CONTEXT → PLAN → APPROVAL. Keep retrieval, draft, recommendation, proposed action, approval, tool use, execution, refusal, and audit as separate accountable states.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
PLACE THE GATE. A PROPOSAL IS NOT PERMISSION. Approval must be explicit, proposal-specific, inspectable, and revocable before any modeled tool step.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
PRESERVE THE STOP. OUT OF SCOPE MEANS REFUSED. Missing context, denied approval, or an out-of-scope tool produces a visible hold or refusal—not invented authority.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
BOUND THE RESULT. SIMULATION HAS ZERO SIDE EFFECTS. No real people, personal data, accounts, credentials, tools, messages, files, transactions, advice, or external actions appear.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
SAVE THIS. MAKE ACTION ACCOUNTABLE. AN ACTION RUNTIME IS GOVERNED WHEN EVERY TRANSITION CARRIES SCOPE, AUTHORITY, APPROVAL, OUTCOME, RECOVERY, AND AN AUDITABLE STOP.

